---
import "../styles/global.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="A technical brewing workspace for homebrewers who care about the details." />
    <title>For Homebrewers — Demleme</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="wordmark" href={base} aria-label="Demleme home">demleme<span>.</span></a>
      <nav class="desktop-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href={`${base}homebrewers`}>Homebrewers</a><a href={`${base}breweries`}>Breweries</a><a href={`${base}#approach`}>Our approach</a></nav>
      <a class="header-cta" href={`${base}#audience-paths`}>All brewing paths <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <details class="mobile-menu"><summary aria-label="Open navigation menu"><span></span><span></span></summary><nav aria-label="Mobile navigation"><a href={`${base}homebrewers`}>Homebrewers</a><a href={`${base}breweries`}>Breweries</a><a href={`${base}#approach`}>Our approach</a></nav></details>
    </header>
    <main>
      <section class="shell audience-page-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> FOR HOME BREWERS</p>
        <h1>Make every brew a <em>learning experience.</em></h1>
        <p>Explore the technical details behind recipes, ingredients and brewing notes. Demleme is being shaped for brewers who want to understand their process, not just follow a set of numbers.</p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href={`${base}#audience-paths`}>Explore Demleme <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </section>
      <!-- IMAGE SLOT: HOMEBREWERS-HERO | Replace placeholder with licensed documentary-style photo of a homebrewer working on a batch. -->
      <section class="shell audience-hero">
        <div class="image-placeholder" data-image-slot="homebrewers-hero"><strong>IMAGE PLACEHOLDER · HOMEBREWERS-HERO</strong><span>Homebrewer measuring, preparing ingredients or working beside a small-batch setup</span></div>
      </section>
      <section class="audience-page-section section-pad">
        <div class="shell audience-page-grid">
          <div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> A MORE CONSIDERED PROCESS</p><h2>Know what goes into every decision.</h2><p>Homebrewing is part craft, part measurement. A useful workspace should make the details easier to follow without getting between you and the brew.</p></div>
          <div><ul class="audience-page-list"><li>Recipe details and ingredient context</li><li>Brewing calculations and clear terminology</li><li>Batch observations and process learning</li></ul><p class="audience-page-note">Areas of focus: clarity, consistency and curiosity — not complexity for its own sake.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="closing-section section-pad"><div class="shell closing-inner"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> THE CRAFT IS IN THE DETAILS</p><h2>Keep learning with <em>every batch.</em></h2><a class="button button-primary" href={base}>Back to Demleme <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer"><div class="shell footer-main"><a class="wordmark footer-wordmark" href={base}>demleme<span>.</span></a><p>Technical brewing software for people who care about the details.</p><a class="back-top" href={base}>Home ↑</a></div><div class="shell footer-bottom"><span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Demleme</span><span>Made for the craft of brewing.</span></div></footer>
  </body>
</html>
